        "id": "1788542299577",
        "role": "assistant",
        "title": "Number of tracks (total and distinct) purchased/listened by each customer",
        "content": "Join Invoice → InvoiceLine to get each track purchase, then join Customer to attach names. Group by customer and compute the sum of Quantity (total tracks listened/purchased) and the count of distinct TrackId values (unique tracks). The result is ordered by the total number of tracks per customer.",
        "sql": "# R code using DBI and dplyr\nlibrary(DBI)\nlibrary(RSQLite)\nlibrary(dplyr)\n\n# Connect to the SQLite database (adjust path as needed)\ncon <- dbConnect(RSQLite::SQLite(), \"Chinook_Sqlite.sqlite\")\n\ncustomer_tracks <- tbl(con, \"Invoice\") %>%\n  inner_join(tbl(con, \"InvoiceLine\"), by = \"InvoiceId\") %>%\n  inner_join(tbl(con, \"Customer\"), by = \"CustomerId\") %>%\n  group_by(CustomerId, FirstName, LastName) %>%\n  summarise(\n    total_tracks = sum(Quantity, na.rm = TRUE),\n    distinct_tracks = n_distinct(TrackId),\n    .groups = \"drop\"\n  ) %>%\n  arrange(desc(total_tracks)) %>%\n  collect()\n\nprint(customer_tracks)\n\n# Remember to close the connection when done\ndbDisconnect(con)",
